  "aiContextParagraph": "As discussions surrounding the potential successor for the vice presidency gain traction, Deputy Speaker of the House of Representatives Sufmi Dasco Ahmad has formally responded to the discourse. Various stakeholders, including regional DPD senators, representatives from the Gerindra party, and labor organizations such as the KSPSI, have expressed support for his potential nomination. Proponents suggest that Dasco possesses the communication abilities and administrative experience necessary to serve effectively in the role. In his response, Dasco maintained that the public should prioritize respecting the constitutional rights and prerogatives of the President, who is responsible for nominating candidates for consideration by the People's Consultative Assembly. Observers note that the current political climate has prompted interest in selecting a candidate who can function as a skilled technocrat and a bridge between political parties and civil society.",
